    {
      "id": 489510,
      "username": "Archana-1230",
      "name": "Archana 1230",
      "created_at": "2025-12-24T16:25:52.994Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Process Loss in ERPNext is conceptually meant for measurable / continuous quantities.<br>\nFor items with Stock UOM = Nos, loss is inherently discrete, not percentage-based.<br>\nBecause of this, fractional loss is logically invalid and ERPNext blocks it by design.<br>\nIt’s best to treat process loss and count-based rejection as different concepts and align BOM design accordingly, rather than forcing percentages on whole-number items.</p>",
